ng it as the top-left coordinate for the next one. The size is preserved in Example 2, and Example 3 confirms that placement is done left to right. Now I believe I can accurately predict the placement of shapes.\n\n\n**Tracing Shape Placement**\n\nMy current focus is on the test input, specifically, tracing the shape placement based on derived logic. I've successfully identified and characterized distinct shapes by color and size, and I'm now mapping each shape's position within the grid. This involves calculating bounding boxes and tracing their placements relative to one another. I'm verifying the application of the placement rules discovered earlier.\n\n\n**Constructing the Output**\n\nI am now generating the output grid based on the derived placement logic. I've calculated the start positions and sizes for each shape. I'm populating the grid row by row, incorporating the appropriate color codes for each cell. I am also making sure that if two colors occupy the same cell, the correct shape is rendered. I am getting ready to visualize the final result!\n\n\n",
